        <body>
            <div xml:id="d309">

                <pb facs="0480" n="380" sameAs="frus:frus1934v02/pg380"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">862.51/4115: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Germany</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Dodd</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-07-14T14:00:00-04:00">July 14, 1934—2 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>92. Your 141, July 13, 6 p.m. The note sent you by Billow yesterday, despite its
                    friendly tone, indicates that the German Government has not altered its basic
                    position in any essential. In particular, it still makes payments under the
                    original contracts dependent upon new commitments, to be made not by the
                    original holders but by this Government, and its conception of equality of
                    treatment is only predicated upon substituted obligations of a different
                    character from the original obligations. In the circumstances, I feel that you
                    should without delay present the <hi rendition="#italic">aide-mémoire</hi>
                    contained in our 90, July 12, 10 p.m., with the following modification:</p>
                <p>Please omit entire paragraph 5, beginning “it would be unwise” and ending
                    “rapidly grow in intensity”,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
